What:		/sys/class/accel/accel<idx>/device/ane_stats
Date:		October 2026
KernelVersion:	7.1
Contact:	Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
		Cumulative Apple Neural Engine (ANE) producer counters for
		this device, one ASCII "key value" pair per line, mode
		0444 (readable without root):

		busy_ns: nanoseconds the engine was busy since the
		device was bound, sampled with a consistent
		close/open snapshot. A busy period opens
		when the first submission lands on an idle
		engine and closes when the last one
		completes; its whole span folds once at
		close, and overlapping submissions share
		the period, so a serialized engine
		(ane.ko, behind engine_lock) reports
		sum(end - start) and a parallel engine
		(ane_t6021) reports the union, never the
		sum. The show callback adds the live tail
		of the still-open period, so the value
		advances while engine work is in flight.

		jobs: completed engine submissions since the
		device was bound. On ane.ko every ANE_SUBMIT
		counts (one per libane ane_exec, N per
		ane_exec_loop). On ane_t6021 only
		CSNE_CMD_PROCEDURE_CALL counts (one per
		engine PROCEDURE_CALL); the control-plane
		exchanges that ride the same path
		(LOAD_PROGRAM, CREATE_PROCESS,
		CH_PROPERTY_WRITE, install-time CONFIG_GET)
		and the boot transport are not engine
		work and are not counted. A submission
		that completes with an error still
		completes its begin/complete pair, so the
		counter stays balanced.

		Neither counter resets while the device is bound.

		The file exists only when the module parameter
		ane.stats / ane_t6021.stats (default 1) is set at
		probe. With stats=0 the driver creates no stats files
		and the submission hot path skips the counters.

Users:		performance samplers that compute engine utilization
		and job rate from the two counters.


